The clerk's stylus stops mid-stroke. Behind the desk, a bored guard shifts his weight and studies the ceiling, suddenly very interested in it. The clerk checks a slate she clearly did not need to check. <npc>"Since before my shift,"</npc> she says. <npc>"Nobody here will log the hull number, and nobody wants it asked twice."</npc> She turns the slate face-down and waits to see what you do with that.

