"Mind the third bell," Tamsin says, her voice thin through the static. "Come when the ring is quiet." The comm clicks dead. Behind you, the dockhand has returned, and the man with him wears no ring badge. He stops at the edge of the desk and looks at the torn crate. The guard's chair is still empty. The stranger says nothing, and he does not look away from you.

